; Add the Kempston joystick to the control bits
;
; Reached only by falling through from #R$A28F when it holds a NOP. Reads the Kempston port and keeps right, left,
; down and fire (bits 0, 1, 2 and 4); joystick up (bit 3) is ignored. Fire lands in bit 4, the second JUMP bit, so it
; jumps like the JUMP key. The bits are ORed into the keyboard result and stored in #R$A2CF.
; .
; Hardware: reads the Kempston joystick port $1F.
;
; E Keyboard control bits from #R$A271
; O:A Control bits, also stored in #R$A2CF
@label=ReadKempston
@isub=LD BC,PORT_KEMPSTON
c$A290 LD BC,$001F   ;
 $A293 IN A,(C)      ;
@isub=AND KEMPSTON_MASK
 $A295 AND $17       ; right, left, down, fire
 $A297 OR E          ;
 $A298 LD ($A2CF),A  ;
 $A29B RET           ;
